>

<p>W.W. Wood Products formally launched its <strong>Nevara</strong> product line on <strong>March 27, 2026</strong>. Nevara is a <strong>frameless, all-plywood</strong> cabinet line built to fill the price gap below Shiloh and Eclipse — so you can keep the budget-driven job in your showroom instead of losing it to an in-stock box.</p>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/nevara-cabinets-launch-2026/nevara-white-shaker-kitchen.webp" alt="White shaker-style Nevara frameless kitchen with a painted island, matching range hood, subway tile backsplash, and brass hardware" width="1600" height="1066" fetchpriority="high" />
</div>

<h2>What Nevara is built to deliver</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>A lower price point</strong> than W.W. Wood's existing lines.</li>
  <li><strong>A strong, streamlined SKU offering</strong> — enough to design a complete kitchen, without a catalog that takes a week to learn.</li>
  <li><strong>Shorter lead times</strong> — estimated at <strong>3–4 weeks</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Frameless, all-plywood construction</strong> — the construction story you'd expect from a W.W. Wood product, at an entry price.</li>
</ul>

<p>The brand site went live at launch: <a href="https://www.nevaracabinets.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.nevaracabinets.com</a>.</p>

<h2>Pricing: Nevara has its own multiplier</h2>

<p>This is the part dealers most need to get right. With the launch, <strong>Nevara uses a dedicated multiplier</strong>, separate from every other product line's multiplier. It must be used whenever you quote a Nevara order. Your Pinnacle Sales rep can confirm your Nevara multiplier.</p>

<div class="spec-table-wrap">
  <table class="spec-table">
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Effective</th><td>All orders placed after <strong>March 27, 2026 at 2:00 PM Central</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Price book</th><td><strong>Nevara Pricing &amp; Specification v2.0</strong></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p><strong>Pre-launch accounts:</strong> if you had early access to Nevara, you must move to the new multiplier <em>and</em> the v2.0 price book. Both replace the early-access pricing and multiplier you were using before launch. If you have older quotes built on early-access pricing, re-run them before they go to a client.</p>

<h2>Resources — where to get them</h2>

<p>The following are available through the W.W. Wood Customer Portal:</p>

<ul>
  <li>PDF Spec Book v2.0</li>
  <li>Cyncly / Design Flex (2020) catalog</li>
  <li>PDF order forms</li>
  <li>PDF literature / brochure</li>
</ul>

<p>W.W. Wood included a hard copy of the Nevara Pricing &amp; Specification v2.0 catalog with its launch notice; additional copies can be ordered if you need them for your team. Need Portal access or help finding the downloads? See our <a href="/playbook/ww-wood-dealer-resources-portal/">dealer resources and Portal access guide</a>.</p>

