  <img src="/images/blog/nevara-cabinets-launch-2026/nevara-kitchen-2.webp" alt="White shaker Nevara L-shaped kitchen with a painted island, pendant lights, and patterned cement-look tile backsplash" width="1600" height="1066" loading="lazy" />
</div>

<h2>Where Nevara wins in your showroom</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Budget-driven remodels</strong> — homeowners comparing you against big-box or in-stock cabinetry who still want plywood construction.</li>
  <li><strong>Builder and multifamily work</strong> — a streamlined SKU set and a 3–4 week estimated lead time are what production schedules need.</li>
  <li><strong>Secondary spaces on a Shiloh or Eclipse job</strong> — laundry, garage, and utility rooms where the client wants W.W. Wood quality without paying the primary-kitchen price.</li>
  <li><strong>A clear Good / Better / Best ladder</strong> — Nevara, Eclipse, and Shiloh from one manufacturer and one rep gives you a three-step price conversation without switching vendors.</li>
</ul>

<h2>A note on our earlier Nevara post</h2>

<p>Our <a href="/playbook/nevara-cabinetry/">July 2025 Nevara overview</a> was written before the formal launch. Two things in it are now out of date: Nevara no longer runs on your Shiloh and Eclipse multipliers (it has its own, above), and the estimated lead time is now 3–4 weeks. Use this post for current quoting rules.</p>

